## Machine access

Everything on this site is available without a browser:

- **Markdown mirror** — every `X.html` has an `X.md` twin at the same path, with the same sections and the same links (to other `.md` pages). You are reading one. Charts are replaced by a link to the JSON series they draw.
- **Atom feeds** — one entry per detected change: [feeds/all.xml]({{ nav_prefix }}feeds/all.xml) (latest {{ FEED_CAP }}), and one per endpoint, model, provider and organization at `feeds/<kind>/<slug>.xml`, linked from each page. Subscribe in any feed reader, or point an RSS-to-email service at one.
- **JSON** — the same files the HTML pages fetch: [data/overview.json]({{ nav_prefix }}data/overview.json) (stats, hero, latest changes, every endpoint row, provider rows), [data/changes.json]({{ nav_prefix }}data/changes.json) (every detected change, newest first), [data/changes_page.json]({{ nav_prefix }}data/changes_page.json) (the change log with descriptions), [data/spend.json]({{ nav_prefix }}data/spend.json), `data/models/<slug>.json` (per-model: every endpoint's full drift / TV series and changes), `data/providers/<slug>.json` (per-provider rates, variants, endpoints), `data/b3it/<slug>/b3it.json` (per-endpoint border-input state). Each page's header names the JSON it was rendered from.
- **Raw data** — every collected response, committed hourly: {{ DATA_REPO_URL }}. The generator that turns it into this site: {{ CODE_REPO_URL }}.

Endpoint slugs are stable: `<model>#<provider>` with every character outside `{{ SLUG_KEPT_CHARS }}` replaced by its two-digit hex code — `/` → `2f`, `#` → `23`, `:` → `3a` (so `moonshotai/kimi-k3:free` at `chutes/fp8` is `moonshotai2fkimi-k33afree23chutes2ffp8`); its page is `endpoints/<slug>.md`.

